played out across countries and generations but also within the life of a single family, as the fortune and the factory passed from generation to generation. The author, Rich Cohen, a grandson (disinherited, and thus set free, along with his mother and siblings), has sought the truth of this rancorous, colorful history, mining thousands of pages of court documents and conducting interviews with members of his extended family.--From publisher description."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Rich Cohen."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":[{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us-ny"},{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us---"}]},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Eisenstadt family"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Eisenstadt, Benjamin"},"topic":"Family"},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Cohen family"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Cohen, Rich"},"topic":"Family"},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"corporate","namePart":"Cumberland Packing Corporation"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Sweet 'N Low (Trademark)"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Businessmen","geographic":"United States","genre":"Biography"},{"@authority":"lcsh","geographic":"Brooklyn (New York, N.Y.)","genre":"Biography"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"CT274.E375 C64 2006"},{"@edition":"22","@authority":"ddc","#text":"929/.2/0973"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0374272298 (hardcover : alk. paper)"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780374272296"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^2005015730"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"60668978"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990099199930203941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000123374118","#text"